<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Premium Prop lifts half-yr distribution.</title>
<headline>Premium Prop lifts half-yr distribution.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Distribution per linked unit (cts)</p>
<p>    - interest		7.06	  vs 5.53</p>
<p>    - dividend		0.14	  vs 0.11</p>
<p>    Income after tax	0.59	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.71	  vs 0.23</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.11	  vs 0.11</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   13.88	 vs 13.12</p>
<p>    Turnover		  29.97	 vs 26.58</p>
<p>Distribution payable November 11</p>
<p>on register October 25</p>
<p>Full name: Premium Properties Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it had capital commitments of about five million rand which would be funded through borrowings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
